e of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids in Vermilion County came in under 90% of normal in November to December 35 times in the 75 years since 1951. In 2025 the middle ran 29% of normal in January to February and 56% in August to September. Grids 24169 and 24469 had their driest year on record in 2025, at 68% of normal. So far in 2026 the middle swung the other way, at 197% of normal in March to April.</p>"}
